# P1b-CTL (CONTROL, PRODUCTION BYTES): lifecycle-evict on the production audited profile and base image (see P1a-CTL). READ: abort-while-waiting and abort-during-hit-prefill "aborted as intended" exactly twice, flood eviction clean,
# reset_prefix_cache, the kill switch latched with nothing published, the in-place restart, returning turns byte-equal to cold. ANY FAIL HERE IS A PRODUCTION FINDING (ALERT line, owner decides after the window).
# The abort-during-hit-prefill drill splits only when other seats decode: the route ledger of the aborted request needs at least two steps, else the Lever N reading of it is NOT_EXERCISED (a whole-step abort is still the production reading).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production image: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=lifecycle-evict
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
